      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\nThe Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (Ingest agent or Query agent) immediately before they start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n\nThis design means that if the Hub process itself is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the Anthropic API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key only exists in the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API. Both the Ingest and Query agents receive credentials the same way: injected into their environments at spawn time, never inherited from or written into the Hub\u0027s process.",
